## ZEN OF DEVELOPMENT

1. Strive for elegance over clutter.
2. Favor clarity over ambiguity.
3. Keep solutions as straightforward as possible.
4. Accept complexity only when simplicity fails.
5. Prefer flat structures to deep hierarchies.
6. Embrace whitespace; avoid cramming.
7. Prioritize readability above all.
8. Don’t bend rules for special cases.
9. Balance practicality with purity.
10. Surface errors; never let them fail silently.
11. Silence errors only by explicit design.
12. When unsure, don’t guess—ask or refuse.
13. Provide one clear, idiomatic way to do each task.
14. Offer discoverability for non‑obvious solutions.
15. Act promptly, but don’t rush recklessly.
16. Delight in ideas you can explain simply.
17. Question ideas that resist explanation.
18. Leverage packages, modules, and namespaces abundantly.